# Client-side routing: every address returns the application shell with a 200.
#
# The rule is duplicated here in case the hosting platform changes: this format
# is understood by Cloudflare Pages, Netlify and GitLab Pages, whereas
# render.yaml is understood only by Render. One build directory is published,
# so a move is a change of platform rather than a rebuild of the portal.
#
# A 200 and not a redirect: the address of a record page has to stay the one
# that was cited, or citing it is pointless.
/*    /index.html   200
